      "steps": [
        "f(x) + a: shift UP by a",
        "f(x) − a: shift DOWN by a",
        "f(x + a): shift LEFT by a",
        "f(x − a): shift RIGHT by a",
        "−f(x): reflect in x-axis; f(−x): reflect in y-axis"
      ],
      "title": "Graph Transformations",
      "content": "<p>Transformations change the position or shape of a graph:</p><p><strong>\\(y = f(x) + a\\):</strong> Translate up by \\(a\\).</p><p><strong>\\(y = f(x + a)\\):</strong> Translate left by \\(a\\) (opposite direction!).</p><p><strong>\\(y = -f(x)\\):</strong> Reflect in the x-axis.</p><p><strong>\\(y = f(-x)\\):</strong> Reflect in the y-axis.</p><p><strong>\\(y = af(x)\\):</strong> Vertical stretch, scale factor \\(a\\).</p><p><strong>\\(y = f(ax)\\):</strong> Horizontal stretch, scale factor \\(\\frac{1}{a}\\).</p>",
      "example": "<p><strong>Describe the transformation from \\(y = x^2\\) to \\(y = (x - 3)^2 + 2\\).</strong></p><p>Translation 3 right and 2 up, or \\(\\binom{3}{2}\\).</p>"
    },
